    "created_at": "2019-09-30T13:55:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-30T14:02:14Z",
    "body": "You can read from `~/.aws/config`. When `AWS_PROFILE` is not present, the region is stored in `[default]` section. Otherwise it's stored in the corresponding `[profile name]` section.\r\n\r\nFor example, when `AWS_PROFILE` is `foo`, the region can be found with\r\n\r\n```\r\ncat ~/.aws/config | sed -nr \"/^\\[profile foo\\]/ { :l /^region[ ]*=/ { s/.*=[ ]*//; p; q;}; n; b l;}\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm sure you can implement that in Rust to be very performant.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
